// The EMITTING config. tsconfig.json stays `noEmit` for the editor and for
// `npm run typecheck`; this one is what `npm run build` uses to produce the
// `dist/` that `npm pack` ships.
//
// Three overrides and one exclude, each load-bearing:
//   - `noEmit: false`                  — the whole point.
//   - `allowImportingTsExtensions`     — TS forbids it whenever emit is on.
//   - `declaration`                    — package.json points `types` at
//                                        dist/index.d.ts; without this there is
//                                        no such file and consumers get `any`.
//   - the `exclude`                    — without it `dist/` carries every
//                                        *.test.js, the jsdom test-setup and the
//                                        11MB bench-report fixture. Confirmed by
//                                        the R125 probe, which shipped all three.
//
// No `declarationMap` and no `sourceMap`: `files` ships `dist` only, so a map
// pointing at `../src/…` would dangle in every consumer. Ship `src` too if you
// ever want them back.
//
// `types: []` drops the base config's `@testing-library/jest-dom` global
// augmentation: it is a devDependency, so a consumer typechecking against our
// .d.ts files must not be told to look for it.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": false,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": false,
    "declaration": true,
    "rootDir": "src",
    "outDir": "dist",
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": [
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.tsx",
    "src/__fixtures__",
    "src/test-setup.ts"
  ]
}
